    "body": "## Purpose\r\n`test_qwen2_5_vl_window_attention_image` and `test_qwen2_5_vl_window_attention_image_batch` set `cudagraph_mm_encoder=True` unconditionally. This PR makes that opt-in a no-op on XPU for 3 reasons:\r\n\r\n#### 1.  On XPU the two cudagraph settings end up inconsistent\r\n`XPUPlatform.check_and_update_config` forces `cudagraph_mode = NONE` unless `VLLM_XPU_ENABLE_XPU_GRAPH=1`, but it does not touch `cudagraph_mm_encoder`. The multimodal CI job runs without that env var, so both of these appear in the same run:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nWARNING [xpu.py:301]               XPU Graph is disabled by environment variable\r\nINFO    [encoder_cudagraph.py:268] Encoder CUDA graph capture complete. Captured 7 graphs across 1 paths.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe resulting *decoder eager + encoder captured* combination is not something XPU enables on its own, and it seems unlikely to be what users would configure in practice, so the coverage it provides on XPU looks limited.\r\n\r\n#### 2. These two tests do not carry the platform guard used by the dedicated ViT CG suite\r\nBoth tests were added in #40830 together with the Qwen2.5-VL `SupportsEncoderCudaGraph` implementation, so their subject is ViT CUDA graph capture on the window-attention path.\r\n\r\nThe same PR also touched the dedicated ViT CG suite, `tests/models/multimodal/generation/test_vit_cudagraph.py`, and there the platform restriction is present. (see https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/7d99c2c4fd61cdeebd29cc7b60584bad10d1ef99/tests/models/multimodal/generation/test_vit_cudagraph.py#L472)\r\n\r\nThe two tests in `test_qwen2_5_vl.py` cover the same feature but do not carry that guard. This PR brings them in line with that suite.\r\n\r\n#### 3. XPU graph has its own CI job\r\nXPU graph support exists and is actively tested. `.buildkite/intel_jobs/test-intel.yaml` defines an `XPU Graph` job that exports `VLLM_XPU_ENABLE_XPU_GRAPH=1`, with `source_file_dependencies` covering exactly the XPU graph surface.\r\n\r\nThat job is where ViT CG coverage on XPU belongs, mirroring how `test_vit_cudagraph.py` is the home for it on cuda/rocm. It already follows an incremental-enablement style, so adding a multimodal case there is straightforward once that support is ready.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npytest -v -s models/multimodal/generation/test_qwen2_5_vl.py -m core_model\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\nAll 12 `core_model` items pass on XPU. The two `window_attention*` tests now log `Skipping encoder and decoder CUDA graph capture` instead of `Encoder CUDA graph capture complete. Captured 7 graphs across 1 paths.`\r\n\r\n## AI Assistance\r\nAI assistance was used for the PR description.\r\n",
