    {
      "body": "@faaany @zhenwei-intel is this still expected after we upgrade to torch 2.14? I would assume that xpu graph should also cover encoder attention part.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-21T01:11:50Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57812#issuecomment-5754124676",
      "id": 5754124676,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-21T01:11:50Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "yma11"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "> @faaany @zhenwei-intel is this still expected after we upgrade to torch 2.14? I would assume that xpu graph should also cover encoder attention part.\r\n\r\nAgreed that ViT xpu graph should be covered. My concern is where. \r\n\r\nThe multimodal job runs without `VLLM_XPU_ENABLE_XPU_GRAPH` and results in `decoder eager, encoder captured` configuration, which is not the original intend for this test. Also, there is a dedicated `XPU Graph` job, where we can cover the ViT xpu graph on XPU. \r\n \r\nHappy to add a multimodal case to the XPU Graph job in this PR or a follow-up.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-21T01:43:06Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57812#issuecomment-5754331932",
      "id": 5754331932,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-21T01:47:46Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "faaany"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "> > @faaany @zhenwei-intel is this still expected after we upgrade to torch 2.14? I would assume that xpu graph should also cover encoder attention part.\r\n> \r\n> Agreed that ViT xpu graph should be covered. My concern is where.\r\n> \r\n> The multimodal job runs without `VLLM_XPU_ENABLE_XPU_GRAPH` and results in `decoder eager, encoder captured` configuration, which is not the original intend for this test. Also, there is a dedicated `XPU Graph` job, where we can cover the ViT xpu graph on XPU.\r\n> \r\n> Happy to add a multimodal case to the XPU Graph job in this PR or a follow-up.\r\n\r\nViT should be supported with torch2.14 + graph.\r\n\r\n`VLLM_XPU_ENABLE_XPU_GRAPH`  will be removed after torch2.14 in this pr https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51600\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-09-21T01:55:44Z",
